:meth:`vBinary.from_xcal <icalendar.prop.binary.vBinary.from_xcal>` now rejects non-canonical Base64 such as ``MTIz=``, whose length is not a multiple of 4, instead of silently decoding it to ``b'123'``. This makes xCal parsing consistent with the strict validation already applied to the iCalendar path (:rfc:`4648#section-4`) and raises :exc:`~icalendar.error.XCalParsingError` as the test suite already expected. I used AI to assist me with this change. @linluozi
